      "type": "prose",
      "heading": "Who Graeme is",
      "html": "<p>Graeme Clark is a Director at Ethos Safety, a health and safety consultancy. These are the full words of four short films in which he describes writing up site inspections with Quickler. Each film is under 40 seconds.</p><p><a href=\"/graeme/\">Back to Graeme Clark's page, with the films</a></p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "heading": "“A fifth, if not a sixth of the time.”",
      "html": "<p><strong>0:00</strong> Then think for three or four sentences and give that to Quickler as a voice note.</p><p><strong>0:04</strong> And that is so efficient that we're maybe only spending a fifth, if not a sixth of the time actually doing the task.</p><p><strong>0:13</strong> We spend the rest of the remaining time interacting with people, which is what we're there to do.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "heading": "“On average, between five to ten minutes.”",
      "html": "<p><strong>0:00</strong> So now compared to before, the beauty with Quickler is we actually can see how long it takes to edit the report.</p><p><strong>0:07</strong> It's taking, on average, between five to ten minutes.</p><p><strong>0:11</strong> And some of this is actually because we've chosen to leave the activity of adding certain things until we go back to the office.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "heading": "“Really working in the field without any sort of support.”",
      "html": "<p><strong>0:00</strong> I think it was when we saw it really working in the field without any sort of support.</p><p><strong>0:06</strong> And what I mean by that is we were able to do exactly the same as we did before report wise, but we were able to do it quicker and we were able to do it slicker.</p><p><strong>0:17</strong> So what I mean by that is that we had the ability to actually generate a high quality report that needed very minimal admin or tidying up afterwards.</p><p><strong>0:27</strong> And we were then able to bounce from that job to the next job.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "heading": "“It was deceptively easy.”",
      "html": "<p><strong>0:00</strong> I think it was deceptively easy.</p><p><strong>0:01</strong> And what I mean by deceptively easy is it didn't feel like we were doing enough on site to capture the data that we desired.</p><p><strong>0:12</strong> It felt almost like we weren't putting enough effort in using Quickler because it was deceptively easy to capture the data by purely just describing it or just taking a short series of photographs.</p>"
    },
